  "code_path_risks_covered": [
    "Exact recipe expansion binds 24 exposed bodies, 48 exposed pose templates with new measured phase gates, paired withdrawals, both starts and fresh references.",
    "The current staged command is protected and predicted every interval; no held action or rotation-pattern score can replace a phase command.",
    "An infeasible command withdraws to zero velocity or an inward target inside the fixed 0.08 rad interior band, capped at 0.75 rad/s and existing actuator limits.",
    "Withdrawal pauses phase memory; a feasible command resumes from fresh observations. Planning and batch commit remain atomic.",
    "The applied withdrawal has its own current forecast. Nonconvergence remains a disqualifying model failure, including during the restoring fallback.",
    "The near-limit route computes ground clearance at its actual initial joint pose and exercises both withdrawals for two intervals from both inverted signs and upright.",
    "Full canary replay independently compares compact projection, phase continuity, commands, every native sample and outcome accounting before broader compact use.",
    "Original zero joint-limit/model-failure and five-degree progress criteria remain unchanged. All outcomes stay retained."
  ],
  "not_covered": [
    "A stopping guarantee, native contact-solver equivalence, useful recovery or comparative superiority.",
    "Full trajectory execution or recovery from the two-interval route alone.",
    "Weakened actuators, other terrain, impacts, arbitrary morphology or untouched evaluation groups.",
    "Learned adaptation, beneficial online memory, live Studio recovery, real time or release."
  ],
  "route_horizon_rationale": "Fifteen fresh roles cover five profiles at two inverted signs and upright. A near-limit joint pose makes both withdrawal paths observable immediately; two intervals cover committed phase and current-state continuity. The route does not prove complete trajectories.",
  "audit_growth_justification": "Reuse the shared owner, evaluator, full replay and compact reader. The new policy and paired assessment add controller/phase invariants, recipe expansion and optional response capture fields. Focused controls cover those changed semantics; no new executable campaign auditor.",
  "discovery_limits": [
    "Development material is exposed. No fitting, training authority or held-out generalization.",
    "Each trajectory is assigned to two of 24 bodies. Each body gets four paired recipes and three fresh references per start: 528 six-second episodes.",
    "Preserve every per-start outcome and every paired both-start decision, including joint and model failures; do not pool opposite winners into a candidate.",
    "The six-second screen retains the original progress and joint criteria; useful leads still require distinct fresh twelve-second full-capture confirmation.",
    "Restoration overrides slew as an explicit protection intervention, while retaining actuator speed and force caps and the observed-bound guard. It is not a verified invariant set."
  ],
